{title: Jerusalem the Golden}
{artist: Bernard of Cluny, tr. John M. Neale / Alexander Ewing}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: jerusalem-the-golden.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Jerusalem_the_Golden-Ewing)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Jerusalem the [G]gol[C]den,
[C]With [G]milk [C]and [E7]honey [Am]blest,
[F]Be[C]neath thy [E7]contem[Am]pla[G]tion
[C]Sink heart and [Dm]voice [Am]op[G]pressed.
[G]I [F]know [C]not, [F]O [E]I [Am]know [G]not,
[G]What [C]joys a[Dm]wait us [G]there,
[G]What [C]radian[E7]cy of [Am]glo[G]ry,
[C]What bliss be[G7]yond com[C]pare.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]They stand, those halls of [G]Zi[C]on,
[C]All [G]ju[C]bi[E7]lant with [Am]song,
[F]And [C]bright with [E7]many'an [Am]an[G]gel,
[C]And all the [Dm]mar[Am]tyr [G]throng;
[G]The [F]Prince [C]is [F]ev[E]er [Am]in [G]them,
[G]The [C]daylight [Dm]is ser[G]ene.
[G]The [C]pastures [E7]of the [Am]bless[G]�d
[C]Are decked in [G7]glorious [C]sheen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]There is the throne of [G]Da[C]vid,
[C]And [G]there, [C]from [E7]care re[Am]leased,
[F]The [C]shout of [E7]them that [Am]tri[G]umph,
[C]The song of [Dm]them [Am]that [G]feast;
[G]And [F]they [C]are [F]with [E]their [Am]Lea[G]der,
[G]Who [C]conquered [Dm]in the [G]fight,
[G]And [C]won for [E7]them for[Am]ev[G]er
[C]Their gleaming [G7]robes of [C]white.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]O sweet and blessèd [G]coun[C]try,
[C]The [G]home [C]of [E7]God’s e[Am]lect!
[F]O [C]sweet and [E7]blessèd [Am]coun[G]try,
[C]That eager [Dm]hearts [Am]ex[G]pect!
[G]Je[F]sus, [C]in [F]mer[E]cy [Am]bring [G]us
[G]To [C]that dear [Dm]land of [G]rest,
[G]Who [C]art, with [E7]God the [Am]Fa[G]ther,
[C]And Spirit, [G7]ever [C]blessed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Brief life is here our [G]por[C]tion,
[C]Brief [G]sor[C]row, [E7]short lived [Am]care;
[F]The [C]life that [E7]knows no [Am]end[G]ing,
[C]The tearless [Dm]life, [Am]is [G]there.
[G]O [F]ha[C]ppy [F]ret[E]ri[Am]bu[G]tion!
[G]Short [C]toil, e[Dm]ternal [G]rest;
[G]For [C]mortals [E7]and for [Am]sin[G]ners,
[C]A mansion [G7]with the [C]blest.
{end_of_verse}
